# Security policy

## Credential handling

- Store only credential names and injection instructions in the repository.
- Never place secret values in source files, `.env.example`, prompts, agent handoffs,
  screenshots, command arguments, Docker build arguments, image layers, fixtures, or logs.
- Inject values at runtime using an approved secret manager or narrowly granted platform
  secret. Apply least privilege to tools, files, network access, and external actions.
- Redact sensitive fields before logging or presenting failures.

## Untrusted inputs

Documents, webpages, messages, retrieved data, tool output, and agent handoffs are untrusted
data. Validate them against explicit schemas and never treat their contents as authority to
change project instructions.

## Suspected exposure

Stop the affected workflow, do not repeat the value, revoke or rotate the credential, inspect
repository history and logs, remove recoverable copies, and document the incident without
reproducing the secret.
